      "value": "<p>A single small rocky moon, locked, cratered and geologically finished. It raises a tide of about four centimetres in the ocean under the ice, which is the largest regular motion that ocean has. The inhabitants of the world below have no word for it, never having seen it, though they have a word for the tide.</p>",
